      "mathematicalReason": "The inscribed angle at A gives arc BC=60°. Equal chords AB and AC then give minor arcs AB=AC=150°, and arc AD=120°. If x is arc AG, equality DG=AB permits x=30° or 90°; the condition BG>GA selects x=30°, with BG=120°. Consequently arc GBC=180°, so GC is a diameter. Angles GAF and AGF are both 60°, making AFG equilateral and AF=AG. Triangle AGE is right at A with angle G=60°, so AE=√3 AG. In right triangle AGC, angle C=15°, hence AG/AC=tan(15°)=2−√3. Using the common angle at A, the area ratio is (AF/AB)(AE/AC)=√3(2−√3)²=7√3−12. This validates the cyclic-angle/right-triangle route; the same arc configuration also supports unit-circle coordinates and linear intersections. Similarity of AFE and ABC is not assumed.",
